WEBVTT

00:09.937 --> 00:12.627
Cliff, it's Rudeus.

00:13.447 --> 00:16.407
Come in. It's not locked.

00:24.897 --> 00:26.547
Are you here alone?

00:26.547 --> 00:30.687
Yes. Cliff is getting 
ready for the wedding.

00:31.107 --> 00:36.777
<i>Cliff proposed to Elinalise 
when we left for Begaritt.</i>

00:37.147 --> 00:40.007
<i>That's right. They're getting married.</i>

00:40.647 --> 00:43.427
In any case, congratulations.

00:45.037 --> 00:47.367
Is something bothering you?

00:47.367 --> 00:52.447
Cliff has been so busy lately, I can only 
get him to do me once every three days.

00:53.237 --> 00:57.297
But once your love nest is ready, 
I bet you won't leave it for a week.

00:58.297 --> 01:00.817
How I envy you.

01:00.817 --> 01:04.147
I mean, you're sleeping with 
Sylphie and Roxy at the same time.

01:04.147 --> 01:05.547
Oh, no, no, no!

01:05.547 --> 01:07.687
We're not having threesomes.

01:07.687 --> 01:10.307
What, you're not?

01:10.307 --> 01:13.807
Doing it with a group can be awfully nice.

01:13.807 --> 01:16.007
You ought to try it at least once.

01:17.507 --> 01:20.507
<i>Stop! That's a devil 
whispering in your ear!</i>

01:20.507 --> 01:24.827
<i>Just try suggesting that, and watch 
both of your relationships fall apart!</i>

01:25.237 --> 01:26.927
<i>Don't listen, Rudeus!</i>

01:26.927 --> 01:28.327
<i>Begone, Mara!</i>

01:28.327 --> 01:29.527
If you'd like,

01:29.527 --> 01:33.947
I wouldn't mind laying some 
groundwork with the two of them.

01:34.157 --> 01:36.447
Please do, O great Elinalise!

01:36.447 --> 01:37.837
Goodness.

01:37.837 --> 01:41.497
But there isn't anything in 
that for me, now is there?

01:43.107 --> 01:47.237
What can I do for you?

01:47.687 --> 01:52.297
I believe I've heard tell of a prized 
aphrodisiac in the Asura Kingdom.

01:52.297 --> 01:55.397
Do you even need it?

01:55.397 --> 02:00.187
I'd like Cliff to go at me like a beast, 
at least on our wedding night.

02:01.767 --> 02:05.347
Understood. I'll do what 
I can to get you some.

02:06.377 --> 02:10.487
When I think of Cliff losing 
control because of it...

02:23.247 --> 02:26.177
Do you, Cliff Grimor,

02:26.177 --> 02:31.397
vow to love only Elinalise Dragonroad 
so long as you live?

02:31.397 --> 02:34.637
I vow to love Elinalise 
to the end of my days.

02:34.867 --> 02:38.127
Do you, Elinalise Dragonroad,

02:38.127 --> 02:42.507
vow to love only Cliff Grimor 
so long as you live?

02:42.507 --> 02:46.357
I vow to love Cliff as long 
as there's life in my body.

02:48.757 --> 02:52.957
Then, let husband give wife 
the necklace of Millis.

02:54.617 --> 02:56.847
Lise, bend down a little.

02:56.847 --> 02:58.757
Oh. Do forgive me.

03:02.197 --> 03:05.557
Let wife give husband a 
kiss to seal their vows.

03:05.557 --> 03:06.477
Of course.

03:18.567 --> 03:19.847
O god!

03:19.847 --> 03:25.367
Grant these two eternal love 
and everlasting prosperity!

03:33.077 --> 03:38.997
<b>III</b>

03:33.077 --> 03:38.997
<b><i>Mushoku Tensei</i></b>

03:33.077 --> 03:38.997
<b><b><i>Jobless Reincarnation</i></b></b>

03:41.497 --> 03:43.167
Wasn't that amazing?!

03:43.167 --> 03:45.667
Elinalise looked so pretty!

03:45.667 --> 03:47.537
I'd love to try on that dress!

03:47.757 --> 03:51.937
Do you think all girls dream 
of that kind of thing?

03:51.937 --> 03:58.077
I guess. But our wedding was 
homey and nice in its own way.

03:58.077 --> 03:59.227
That's true.

04:06.817 --> 04:09.747
Would you like to have a 
big wedding, too, Roxy?

04:09.747 --> 04:10.737
No.

04:11.277 --> 04:14.737
<i>Roxy and I didn't have a ceremony.</i>

04:14.737 --> 04:17.037
<i>Apparently it's not a Migurd custom.</i>

04:17.287 --> 04:22.057
<i>Still, I bet seeing that could 
make her want one after all.</i>

04:22.367 --> 04:27.587
I don't need a ceremony, 
but, well... you know?

04:38.237 --> 04:41.287
Pardon me. Your forehead 
was just so beautiful.

04:41.287 --> 04:43.317
Y-You think so?

04:44.417 --> 04:47.177
Me, too, Rudy. Me, too.

04:52.567 --> 04:57.917
Brother, would you stop doing 
things like that in public?

04:57.917 --> 04:59.957
Aw. Feeling left out?

05:00.807 --> 05:03.707
Hey! Stop that!

05:07.147 --> 05:11.667
Oh, honestly. 
How can you be so shameless?

05:11.667 --> 05:12.667
Aisha.

05:14.137 --> 05:15.787
Big Brother!

05:18.337 --> 05:21.717
Aisha, don't you latch on with your legs.

05:21.717 --> 05:22.967
Oh, all right.

05:22.967 --> 05:26.607
Honestly. You're eleven years old.

05:26.607 --> 05:29.757
I wish you would learn to control 
yourself like a proper young lady.

05:29.757 --> 05:32.227
Now, now. We're all family here.

05:32.547 --> 05:34.617
<i>Hang on. Eleven?</i>

05:34.617 --> 05:37.477
I got a kiss from Big Brother.

05:34.957 --> 05:39.667
<i>Is it me, or did no one ever celebrate
their fifth and tenth birthdays?</i>

05:37.477 --> 05:39.667
You're welcome to it.

05:40.357 --> 05:44.577
<i>I doubt Paul got a chance during the 
fallout from the mass teleportation.</i>

05:45.117 --> 05:48.657
We'll have to throw a big party 
with everyone when we get home.

05:49.607 --> 05:51.287
<i>Okay. That settles it.</i>

05:51.827 --> 05:53.467
<i>I'm throwing a party.</i>

06:03.107 --> 06:06.407
The city is always so lively 
this time of year.

06:06.407 --> 06:10.307
Yes. All sorts of people come 
for the harvest festival.

06:10.597 --> 06:13.787
It's the best time to get 
rare goods from abroad;

06:13.787 --> 06:15.987
perfect for finding presents.

06:15.987 --> 06:18.287
I bet they'll both be surprised.

06:18.537 --> 06:21.577
<i>Once I decided to throw 
my sisters a surprise party,</i>

06:21.577 --> 06:24.847
<i>the first thing I did was 
get Sylphie and Roxy involved.</i>

06:24.847 --> 06:29.537
<i>But that's not the only reason 
we're out on the town today.</i>

06:29.887 --> 06:32.747
I laid the groundwork 
for you, as promised.

06:34.867 --> 06:37.727
Rudy? Rudy?

06:38.137 --> 06:39.357
Are you okay?

06:39.357 --> 06:43.347
You're drooling. Are you hungry already?

06:43.347 --> 06:46.887
<i>Whoops. I let my fantasies 
get the better of me.</i>

06:46.887 --> 06:49.877
<i>I'll take the time to pick out 
presents for Norn and Aisha right.</i>

06:49.877 --> 06:52.297
<i>And I'll make sure Sylphie 
and Roxy enjoy our date.</i>

06:52.297 --> 06:53.847
<i>Both parts matter.</i>

06:53.847 --> 06:57.357
Sorry. I suppose my jaw 
went slack for a moment.

06:57.357 --> 06:59.227
Now, what are we waiting for?

07:01.607 --> 07:08.147
This pot that freezes its contents when 
imbued with mana might be good for Aisha.

07:08.147 --> 07:11.857
I think Aisha would like something cuter.

07:11.857 --> 07:13.467
Oh, good point.

07:13.467 --> 07:17.127
Speaking of which, what do 
you think Norn might like?

07:17.397 --> 07:20.157
Norn? I wonder.

07:20.157 --> 07:25.377
She seems to like the same things as boys.
Armor and swords and horses.

07:25.637 --> 07:27.877
Really? I'm surprised you knew that.

07:28.127 --> 07:31.767
I'd like to make friends with her.

07:33.507 --> 07:34.917
Hm...

08:07.187 --> 08:10.547
Sorry for making you help choose 
my clothes on top of everything.

08:10.547 --> 08:14.047
Don't mention it. I had a good time, too.

08:14.637 --> 08:16.507
Don't you think it's 
about time for dinner?

08:17.747 --> 08:20.607
To tell the truth, 
I already made reservations.

08:24.097 --> 08:25.907
I know this place.

08:25.907 --> 08:28.407
My grandma told me about it.

08:28.407 --> 08:32.667
She said to make up with you 
here if we ever had a fight.

08:32.667 --> 08:35.317
What, you, too, Sylphie?

08:35.317 --> 08:39.377
Elinalise told me that Rudy

08:39.377 --> 08:42.387
might invite us both to this inn.

08:42.827 --> 08:46.787
So, then, I mean...

08:48.897 --> 08:50.637
I see how it is.

08:51.637 --> 08:53.827
Rudy's lechery knows no bounds.

08:53.827 --> 08:56.287
<i>It doesn't matter what they say about me.</i>

08:56.287 --> 08:59.897
<i>The great Elinalise has 
already planted the seeds!</i>

08:59.897 --> 09:03.657
Oh, but if we spend the night, 
what about Lucie?

09:03.657 --> 09:06.917
Not to worry. I asked 
Lilia to take care of her.

09:06.917 --> 09:08.467
Just like that?

09:08.467 --> 09:12.037
Well, I do know she'll be 
in good hands with Lilia.

09:12.037 --> 09:17.157
<i>Sylphie probably doesn't like the 
idea of us both being gone overnight.</i>

09:17.157 --> 09:18.917
<i>I know we shouldn't, too.</i>

09:18.917 --> 09:22.577
<i>But, well... I won't make excuses.</i>

09:23.027 --> 09:27.197
<i>I'm sorry, Lucie. Forgive your 
father for caving to his desires.</i>

09:28.427 --> 09:30.717
Now, both of you.

09:30.717 --> 09:31.687
Yes?

09:30.717 --> 09:32.087
What is it?

09:34.637 --> 09:40.427
The thing is... I booked us a room.

09:40.427 --> 09:43.317
<i>That's a line I always wanted 
to say once in my life.</i>

09:46.607 --> 09:47.687
Okay.

09:48.067 --> 09:51.597
Um, Roxy, I know I'm repeating myself,

09:51.597 --> 09:53.987
but you don't mind doing 
it together, do you?

09:53.987 --> 09:56.797
No. I'm fully prepared.

09:56.797 --> 09:58.517
Please be good to me.

10:07.357 --> 10:10.417
<i>This just might be the 
best night of my life.</i>

10:18.777 --> 10:21.717
<i>Today's the day of the 
surprise birthday party.</i>

10:22.237 --> 10:24.607
<i>We have a lot to get ready,</i>

10:24.607 --> 10:28.917
<i>but we've got to get my sisters 
out of the house first.</i>

10:47.237 --> 10:49.137
Oh, there you are.

10:49.137 --> 10:51.087
Roxy, Norn, Aisha.

10:51.087 --> 10:54.127
I'd like a word. Would you 
come with me for a moment?

10:54.127 --> 10:55.587
A word about what?

10:55.587 --> 10:58.307
All right. We'll go with you.

10:59.027 --> 11:01.517
Master Rudeus is inviting you out.

11:01.517 --> 11:03.727
Aisha, go along.

11:14.687 --> 11:16.077
Fishing?

11:16.077 --> 11:19.817
Yes. Just the thing for getting 
to know each other better, right?

11:22.917 --> 11:26.457
<i>Norn still acts standoffish with Roxy.</i>

11:26.457 --> 11:28.867
<i>And Roxy said she wanted to make friends,</i>

11:29.247 --> 11:32.027
<i>so hopefully this will 
bring them closer together.</i>

11:35.717 --> 11:38.817
I've never fished before.

11:38.817 --> 11:40.487
Me, neither! Me, neither!

11:40.927 --> 11:44.197
I've always wanted to try it!

11:46.817 --> 11:50.897
Big Brother, let's see which 
one of us can catch the most!

11:50.897 --> 11:52.937
R-Right! I'm game.

11:52.937 --> 11:56.717
How about the loser has to do one thing 
the winner says, to keep it interesting?

11:56.717 --> 11:57.727
You're on!

12:01.687 --> 12:04.907
Oh, Brother! What do I do with this?

12:06.657 --> 12:08.507
I don't know, either.

12:08.507 --> 12:11.127
After all, I've never 
fished a day in my life.

12:12.897 --> 12:13.987
Um...

12:17.217 --> 12:19.387
Would you like me to teach you?

12:21.917 --> 12:23.767
Yes, please.

12:25.757 --> 12:29.207
Spike the worm on the 
hook without tearing it.

12:30.077 --> 12:34.217
I think we'd better cast at the opposite 
bank from here. Under those trees.

12:34.867 --> 12:36.507
Do you think you can do it?

12:36.507 --> 12:38.077
I'll try.

12:47.737 --> 12:49.547
You're good at this.

12:49.547 --> 12:51.477
Thank you for saying so.

12:55.707 --> 12:57.467
I wish I could do that.

12:57.467 --> 13:03.337
When I was traveling alone, I had to 
catch my own food as often as I could.

13:11.237 --> 13:12.557
That reminds me.

13:12.557 --> 13:16.937
Ruijerd caught fish for us when 
we were traveling with him.

13:16.937 --> 13:18.367
He fishes, too?

13:18.367 --> 13:24.647
No. He'd jab his spear into the water 
and skewer three fish on the tip.

13:25.657 --> 13:28.537
Oh, Norn, you have a bite.

13:29.307 --> 13:30.317
Try pulling.

13:30.317 --> 13:31.207
R-Right!

13:36.117 --> 13:37.937
Yes. That's the way.

13:37.937 --> 13:39.047
Pull! Pull!

13:39.047 --> 13:41.557
Hang in there. Easy does it.

13:49.987 --> 13:53.087
I... I did it! I caught one!

13:53.087 --> 13:54.347
I caught my first fish!

13:54.667 --> 13:57.357
Wow! It's a big one!

13:58.177 --> 14:01.257
<i>It looks like it was only a matter 
of time until they got friendly.</i>

14:01.257 --> 14:02.277
There!

14:02.787 --> 14:04.747
That makes three!

14:10.397 --> 14:14.107
It looks like you haven't been 
doing too well, Big Brother.

14:14.107 --> 14:16.067
Whatever is the matter?

14:16.067 --> 14:17.707
How could this happen?

14:17.707 --> 14:19.507
I wonder what I should make you do.

14:19.507 --> 14:22.997
What if I had you cuddle 
me all night, whispering,

14:22.997 --> 14:25.767
"Aisha, you're the cutest"?

14:26.097 --> 14:29.167
<i>I guess I could live with that.</i>

14:29.167 --> 14:33.947
<i>But wait. Surely I'd better impress 
her with what her big brother can do.</i>

14:35.127 --> 14:37.567
Fish!

14:38.147 --> 14:39.657
All right! It's a big—

14:42.667 --> 14:44.277
Big Brother...

14:44.277 --> 14:47.907
A fisherman has a duty to 
keep his fishing spot clean.

14:48.457 --> 14:51.167
Aisha, I'm about to get serious.

14:51.167 --> 14:53.547
You mean you weren't before?

14:53.547 --> 14:55.087
Just you watch.

15:02.567 --> 15:03.847
Isn't that...

15:03.847 --> 15:08.727
<i>I've been experimenting ever since 
I learned Lightning from Roxy.</i>

15:09.037 --> 15:11.867
<i>The key to this spell is compression.</i>

15:11.867 --> 15:14.827
<i>You spread a ton of mana through 
the sky to make clouds,</i>

15:14.827 --> 15:17.437
<i>then compress them to 
cause a lightning strike.</i>

15:17.977 --> 15:20.947
<i>But if I keep the size of the clouds 
under control from the start,</i>

15:20.947 --> 15:24.067
<i>I can fire off a less powerful shock.</i>

15:24.737 --> 15:25.857
<i>I call it...</i>

15:26.567 --> 15:27.907
<i>Electric!</i>

15:37.947 --> 15:40.977
How about that! I'd call 
that a win for Big Brother!

15:41.297 --> 15:43.707
Big Brother, magic is cheating!

15:43.707 --> 15:44.867
Brother...

15:44.867 --> 15:47.747
Rudy, that wasn't very mature of you.

15:53.717 --> 15:56.687
Look! Look at all the fish I caught!

15:56.687 --> 15:58.627
How'd you do, Norn?

15:59.517 --> 16:03.397
I learned from Roxy and 
caught a fish this big!

16:05.887 --> 16:08.547
Roxy, teach me next time!

16:08.547 --> 16:11.847
No. You caught way more fish anyway.

16:11.847 --> 16:14.867
I need Roxy to teach me again!

16:15.257 --> 16:17.787
Don't fight over me.

16:17.787 --> 16:19.897
I'll teach both of you.

16:21.217 --> 16:22.957
We're home!

16:25.907 --> 16:27.767
Happy birthday!

16:30.147 --> 16:31.887
Happy birthday.

16:30.147 --> 16:31.277
Happy birthday.

16:32.177 --> 16:35.777
Um... We're already eleven, though?

16:35.777 --> 16:39.927
We know. But we didn't get to throw 
you a party when you turned ten.

16:39.927 --> 16:44.077
So, Rudy said, what's wrong 
with doing it a year late?

16:44.077 --> 16:45.897
Big Brother did?

16:45.897 --> 16:47.727
Go on in.

16:55.507 --> 16:56.587
Ahem.

16:57.117 --> 17:00.147
Does everybody have something to drink?

17:01.447 --> 17:04.127
It's been seven years since the 
mass teleportation in Fittoa.

17:04.517 --> 17:07.677
It's been a long time, but our 
family is finally together again.

17:08.427 --> 17:12.507
Dad is gone, and we don't know if 
Mom will ever go back to how she was.

17:13.167 --> 17:17.687
But Dad wouldn't want us to 
stay in mourning forever.

17:18.397 --> 17:23.087
So, I think I—we—ought to smile.

17:23.637 --> 17:26.227
When I met Dad in Begaritt,

17:26.227 --> 17:29.687
I promised him a big party 
if we all got back together.

17:32.067 --> 17:35.847
Let's cut loose and enjoy ourselves 
today, like he would have wanted.

17:38.197 --> 17:39.307
Cheers!

17:39.587 --> 17:41.027
Cheers.

17:44.157 --> 17:48.297
These are for you, from Rudy and us.

17:48.877 --> 17:51.387
We hope you'll like them.

17:51.967 --> 17:53.807
Thank you so much.

18:01.307 --> 18:03.077
Can I open it?!

18:03.077 --> 18:04.537
Of course you can.

18:19.987 --> 18:21.537
I love it!

18:21.537 --> 18:24.427
Look, Norn! I got boots!

18:24.707 --> 18:28.157
You both got wonderful presents.

18:28.477 --> 18:30.087
Look, Mom! Look!

18:30.087 --> 18:31.307
I got a present!

18:31.307 --> 18:34.437
I'll wear it next time 
we go out together, okay?

18:41.797 --> 18:43.947
Did she just smile?

18:46.887 --> 18:48.277
Mom...

18:57.397 --> 18:58.737
My lady...

18:59.297 --> 19:00.537
Thank goodness.

19:07.367 --> 19:10.887
This is from my lady and I 
for the two of you.

19:10.887 --> 19:13.377
Thank you very much, Lilia.

19:13.727 --> 19:17.617
Um, Mom, may I have one, too?

19:17.617 --> 19:20.047
Yes, of course you may.

19:20.047 --> 19:23.737
You're Lord Paul's daughter, too.

19:26.177 --> 19:28.587
Thank you, Mom.

19:31.767 --> 19:35.497
My lady... I hope we'll have 
many more good times together.

19:46.367 --> 19:48.027
Thank you very much.

19:52.817 --> 19:53.967
Roxy.

19:57.597 --> 19:59.717
Yes? What is it?

19:59.717 --> 20:02.647
Here. This is from us to you.

20:02.647 --> 20:05.477
Huh? Oh, uh...

20:05.477 --> 20:06.617
What for?

20:06.617 --> 20:08.267
It's a wedding present.

20:08.267 --> 20:11.117
Roxy, congratulations on 
your marriage to Rudy.

20:11.117 --> 20:12.837
Uh, um...

20:12.837 --> 20:14.497
Go on. Open it.

20:22.117 --> 20:23.457
Is this...

20:23.987 --> 20:28.757
Do you remember when 
I told you I got lucky?

20:28.757 --> 20:29.877
Yes.

20:29.877 --> 20:36.787
If I hadn't met Rudy, I don't think
I'd be standing here alive now.

20:37.277 --> 20:38.837
You're exaggerating.

20:38.837 --> 20:40.387
I am not.

20:40.787 --> 20:44.267
Meeting Rudy changed my life.

20:44.667 --> 20:49.597
So, I'm glad that someone who 
changed his life for the better

20:49.597 --> 20:52.267
loves him, too.

20:54.507 --> 21:00.897
But if Rudy couldn't return her 
feelings because of me, I'd feel—

21:01.737 --> 21:04.037
Oh, I can't find the right words.

21:06.347 --> 21:08.377
So, Roxy,

21:09.507 --> 21:13.427
let's be like Zenith and Lilia.

21:17.997 --> 21:20.837
Thank you... very much.

21:23.467 --> 21:26.227
<i>We're all a big, happy, smiling family.</i>

21:26.947 --> 21:31.057
<i>I'm sure this is what Paul wanted for us.</i>

21:38.227 --> 21:40.277
Bluie-bluie-blah!

21:39.237 --> 21:42.997
Go on, Lucie! Smile!

21:41.617 --> 21:44.107
Aisha, what kind of face is that?

21:46.767 --> 21:50.577
Happy fifth birthday, Rudy!

21:46.767 --> 21:50.577
I wish you a very happy 
birthday, Master Rudeus.

21:50.577 --> 21:52.367
Isn't that great, Lucie?

21:52.367 --> 21:56.267
Let's throw another big party 
when they both turn fifteen.

21:53.487 --> 21:56.957
Peek-a-boo!

21:57.527 --> 21:59.517
Oh, look. She smiled.

21:59.517 --> 22:00.607
Lucie!

22:00.607 --> 22:01.977
She's so cute!

22:01.967 --> 22:04.967
<b>Episode 5
Celebrations</b>

23:34.977 --> 23:40.057
Next Time
Another Domestic Disaster?
